  "title": "Station To Station",
  "country": "UK",
  "released": "1976-01-23",
  "notes": "First issue released with the orange labels and earliest runout matrices.\nIncludes a one-sided insert with printed credits and a plain patent inner.\n\nLater [url=https://www.discogs.com/David-Bowie-Station-To-Station/release/3538833]reissued[/url] with the \"Stereo\" printed mention on labels.\n\nSteve Schapiro's name is correctly credited in a later [url=https://www.discogs.com/David-Bowie-Station-To-Station/release/9810328]reissue[/url].\n\nFront photo from the film 'The Man Who Fell To Earth'. Monochrome version of an original full colour shot. The latter was scheduled to be on the cover, per pre release publicity at the time, but was withdrawn just before the LP’s release and replaced with the black and white picture.\n\nPublishing Info:\nA1 to B2: Bewlay Bros. Music / Chrysalis Music / MainMan Ltd.\nB3: Carlin Music Corp.\nA2: ℗1975\nA1, A3 to B3: ℗1976 RCA Records\n\nRecorded at (uncredited on release) [l267581], Los Angeles.\n\nTrack times not stated on the release.\n\nRCA on sleeve, RCA Victor on labels",
  "released_formatted": "23 Jan 1976",
